### To Reproduce

Create Backend:
```
export const auth = betterAuth({
  database: drizzleAdapter(db, {
    provider: "pg",
    schema: authSchema,
  }),
  advanced: {
    database: {
      generateId: "uuid",
    },
  },
}
```
Generate Migrations:
```
@better-auth/cli@latest generate
```

in the resulting migration:
```
export const session = pgTable(
  "session",
  {
    id: uuid("id").defaultRandom().primaryKey(),
    expiresAt: timestamp("expires_at").notNull(),
    token: text("token").notNull().unique(),
    createdAt: timestamp("created_at").defaultNow().notNull(),
    updatedAt: timestamp("updated_at")
      .$onUpdate(() => /* @__PURE__ */ new Date())
      .notNull(),
    ipAddress: text("ip_address"),
    userAgent: text("user_agent"),
    userId: uuid("user_id")
      .notNull()
      .references(() => user.id, { onDelete: "cascade" }),
    impersonatedBy: text("impersonated_by"),
  },
  (table) => [index("session_userId_idx").on(table.userId)],
);
```
but because i specify `generateId: "uuid",` i believe 
`
    impersonatedBy: text("impersonated_by"),
`
 should be 
`    impersonatedBy: uuid("impersonated_by"),`
 at a minimum, optimally, maybe 
`
impersonatedBy: uuid("impersonated_by").references(() => user.id, { onDelete: "set null" }),
`
because the generated user table looks like this:
```
export const user = pgTable("user", {
  id: uuid("id").defaultRandom().primaryKey(),
  name: text("name").notNull(),
  email: text("email").notNull().unique(),
  emailVerified: boolean("email_verified").default(false).notNull(),
  image: text("image"),
  createdAt: timestamp("created_at").defaultNow().notNull(),
  updatedAt: timestamp("updated_at")
    .defaultNow()
    .$onUpdate(() => /* @__PURE__ */ new Date())
    .notNull(),
  role: text("role"),
  banned: boolean("banned").default(false),
  banReason: text("ban_reason"),
  banExpires: timestamp("ban_expires"),
});
```

(i updated the generated 
`     
id: uuid("id")
    .default(sql`pg_catalog.gen_random_uuid()`)
    .primaryKey(),
`
to be 
`
  id: uuid("id").defaultRandom().primaryKey(),

` 
additionally, you could also leverate the DB for updating timestams as follows:
```
updatedAt: timestamp("updated_at").defaultNow().$onUpdate(() => new Date()).notNull(),
```

